{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["SIAM J. Appl. Dyn. Syst."],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2025,9,30]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>Abstract.<\/jats:p>\n                  <jats:p>In their paper,\u00a0Bakhtin et\u00a0al. [ SIAM J. Appl. Dyn. Syst., 20 (2021), pp. 1917\u20131958] consider a Markov process obtained by random switching between two stable linear vector fields in the plane and characterize the singularities of the invariant density in terms of the switching and contraction rates. This paper considers a generalization of this model obtained by random switching between two stable linear vector fields in [Formula: see text] and provides sufficient conditions ensuring that the invariant distribution is absolutely continuous and has a [Formula: see text] density. In dimension [Formula: see text],\u00a0it provides, to the best of our knowledge, the first fully nonelliptic example of random switching for which quantitative conditions guaranteeing smoothness of the invariant density can be proved.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1137\/24m1696172","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2025,9,22]],"date-time":"2025-09-22T08:00:50Z","timestamp":1758528050000},"page":"2473-2488","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Regularity of Invariant Densities for Random Switching between Two Linear ODEs in \\(\\mathbb{R}^{{d}}\\)"],"prefix":"10.1137","volume":"24","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0003-0703-3107","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Michel","family":"Bena\u00efm","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Institut de Math\u00e9matiques, Universit\u00e9 de Neuch\u00e2tel, Facult\u00e9 des Sciences, 2000 Neuch\u00e2tel, Switzerland."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Am\u00e9thyste","family":"Bichard","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"DER de math\u00e9matiques, ENS Paris-Saclay, 91190 Gif-sur-Yvette, France."}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"auth